{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Lights in the parlor, fire in the grate
Clock on the mantle says [E7]it's getting [A]late
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Curtains on the window, snowy white
The parlor is pleasant on a [E7]Sunday [A]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Ida Red, Ida Red,
[A]I’ma plumb fool about [E7]Ida [A]Red
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Chicken in the bread pan, pecking out dough
Granny will your dog bite? No child, no
Hurry up boys and don't fool around
Grab your partner and truck on down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Lamp on the table, picture on the wall,
There's a pretty sofa and that's not all
If I'm not mistaken and I'm sure I'm right
There's somebody else in the parlor tonight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
My old misses swore to me
When she died she's set me free
She lived so long her head got bald
She took a notion not to die at all
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Lights a burnin' dim, fire's a gettin’ low
Somebody says it's time to go
I hear a whisper, gently and light
Don’t forget to come next Sunday night
{end_of_chorus}
